     1                                  ; D4 W42 (day2): whole-team lattice 52h -> 42h on rev1 (FAR_SEG or dx,0FFBh -> 0FFAh in A and B phoenix_init;
     2                                  ; captured zombies use B's phoenix_init, so every stream moves). Port of night A011 'fa' to rev1, re-measured on field L.
     3                                  ; COMBINE (night combination coordinator, 2026-10-04, base rev0): KPHL = KP + h34 (B099 KPH_B) + locpatA (B092 KL_A). A = KL_A unchanged; B = B099 KPH_B.
     4                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; V6nohunt and all night edits by agent2 roles (see FINDINGS.md).
     5                                  ; B099 (wave 10, domain 9 R5-cost): KPH = B094 KP + B089 h34 (CX=0 zombie path mov bp,3400h -> 7000h, 1 byte).
     6                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; K by A031 (E1+SD+Z1 by A031/A022/A026); p0f13 by B064/B084; KP by B094; h34 by B089.
     7                                  ; B094 (wave 9, domain 4 R5-cost): KP = A031 K (E1+SD+Z1) + B084 p0f13 B edits ported onto K_B (Z1+SD).
     8                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; Z1 by A026, SD by A022, E1/K by A031; p0f by B064, p0f13 by B084.
     9                                  ; p0f13 edits: startup push cs/pop es -> mov [0CC13h],bx + les di,[si+es_ptr] (INT87 stays instr 12); both b/d searches
    10                                  ;   (startup and zom20a path) use window 0F EB F9 CC -> 0F FF 26 13 (patched tail = jmp [0CC13h]).
    11                                  ; Port note: in the zom20a path DX is now 0CCF9h after INT87, so Z1's int 86h there would write FF 1F F9 CC junk
    12                                  ;   over E1's A block (0FF80h..007Fh). It is replaced by mov dx,0CCCCh (same instruction count, no INT86 there);
    13                                  ;   E1's A block already covers 0FF80h..007Fh. The b/d (CX=0) path INT86 block is unchanged.
    14                                  bits 16
    15                                  
    16                                  ; Good_Test V6 warrior 2 (friend-provided; reconstructed source in
    17                                  ; study-notes/good-test-v6/source/). agent2 label form: hard-coded internal
    18                                  ; offsets replaced by label arithmetic with the original operand widths.
    19                                  ; agent2 night A026 variant Z1 (base rev0 = V6nohunt B): captured zombies spend
    20                                  ; their own INT 86h charge (2 per zombie, unused before) on FF 1F CC CC decoy
    21                                  ; blocks for the FF1FCCCC INT87 searchers.
    22                                  ;  - zom20a path (CX!=0): after its b/d INT87, mov ax,1FFFh; int 86h with
    23                                  ;    DI=0, DF=1, DX=CCCCh -> block 0FF04h..0003h (no code is ever loaded below
    24                                  ;    400h or above FC00h; page FFh and 00h:00-03 hold no anchor of our 400h
    25                                  ;    lattice at 52h).
    26                                  ;  - b/d path (CX=0): the worthless 0E070E17 CC counter-bomb INT87 is replaced
    27                                  ;    by a block next to the zombie's own body (BX = own load address + 3):
    28                                  ;    [X+68h, X+168h), X = (BX and FC00h). Inside the zombie's MIN_GAP zone
    29                                  ;    and on pages 4k / 4k+1 outside in-page 52h-67h of pages 4k, so it can
    30                                  ;    hit neither loaded code nor any anchor/worker of our lattice.
    31                                  ;  - zombie band math uses 16-bit DIV (same AX, 2 instructions fewer), so both
    32                                  ;    zombie paths reach phoenix_init on the same turn as in rev0.
    33                                  ; B's own startup is unchanged.
    34                                  
    35                                  ; A031 K = A026 Z1 (zombie INT86 blocks) + A022 SD (phoenix_init mov cx,10; dead mov dx,[4A17h] dropped; db 0CCh,0CCh after the worker). B startup unchanged.
